welcome to the aging phase course  this course has been designed to teach  you all about the early face ecosystem  how to use the data set at model hub as  well as our open source libraries  here is the table of contents as you can  see  it's divided into three sections which  becomes progressively more advanced  at this stage only the first section has  been released  which will teach you the basics of how  to use a transformer model  fine tune it on your own data set and  share the result with the community  we're actively working on the next two  sections  a general timeline wave in mind is to  have section 2 released in the fall  of 2021 and the last section for the end  of 2021  beginning of 2022 was that just  estimates though  don't be married for a bit late the  first chapter requires no technical  knowledge  and is a good introduction to learn what  transferable models can do  and how they could be of use to you or  your company  the next three chapters require a good  knowledge of python  and some basic knowledge of machine  learning and deep learning  if you don't know what a training and  validation set are  or what gradient decent means you should  look at an introductory course  such as the ones published by deep  learning dot ai or fast.ti  it's also best if you have some basics  in one deep learning framework  by torch or tensorflow each part of the  material introduced in this course  has a version in both those frameworks  so we'll be able to pick the one you're  most comfortable with  this is the team that developed this  course i'll now let each of the speakers  introduce themselves briefly  hi my name is matthew and i'm a machine  learning engineer at hugging face  i work on the open source team and i'm  responsible for maintaining particularly  the tensorflow code there  previously i was a machine learning  engineer at parsley who have recently  been acquired by automatic  and i was a postdoctoral researcher  before that at trinity college dublin in  ireland  working on computational genetics and  retinal disease  hi i'm lysander i'm a machine learning  engineer at hugging face i work  specifically on the open source team  i've been at hugging face for a few  years now and i've been working  alongside my team members  on most of the tools that you'll see in  this course  hi i'm silva i'm a research engineer at  talking  dockingface  and one of the main maintainers of the  transformers library  previously i worked at fast.ai where i  helped develop the fastai library  as well as the online mooc before that i  was a math and computer science teacher  in france
 

